# A change here needs the owner's approving review before it merges (the
# ruleset on main requires code-owner review). These are the checks that
# decide a merge and every file they run or import, the scripts that run with
# repository secrets, the hooks and settings that
# refuse an agent's commands, the App's identity, and infra whose apply is a
# human maintenance act. A PR's own run uses its own copy of these files, so
# owning them is what keeps a PR from rewriting its judge; everything else a
# local agent PR merges itself after review (docs/governance.md § What GitHub
# enforces).
/.github/                        @iengai
/scripts/ops/contract.py         @iengai
/scripts/ops/fix_issue.py        @iengai
/scripts/ops/claude_harness.py   @iengai
/scripts/ops/agent_identity.py   @iengai
/scripts/ops/diagnose_issue.py   @iengai
/.claude/skills/verify/scripts/  @iengai
/.claude/hooks/                  @iengai
/.claude/settings*.json          @iengai
/terraform/                      @iengai
